  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 206 PM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge will significantly shift westward to around \nLas Vegas as a positively tilted shortwave moves in from the north \nSaturday. There's a low chance (10-25%)for another round of showers \nand thunderstorms in the far western Panhandles on Saturday, but dry \nair should be moving into the eastern and potentially central \nPanhandles, and this dry air may try to exert some (negative) \ninfluence onto any potential development in the western Panhandles. \nThe most likely scenario is that most, if not all, of the CWA will \nstay dry on Saturday. Temperatures will be merely a few degrees \nwarmer than normal, a welcomed change from the past week and a half. \n\nThe upper-level ridge will begin to extend back toward the east on \nSunday and into early next week. This means we will see temperatures \nwarm back up into the upper-90s to low-100s with likely dry weather. \n\nVanden Bosch",
